1.Go to application and click on register end device on the top right corner.

![End devices list - The Things Stack](hardware/sensors/images/ttn-end-devices-list.png)

2.Select enter device specifics manually and enter the specifics.





3.You can find the specifics on the box.



4.Join EUI is APP EUI from the box




5.Enter the other specifics from the box


6.After filling in the specifics register the end device .
 Press the ACT button for 5 seconds to activate the CS01-LB. The Green LED will blink rapidly 5 times, and the device will enter OTAA mode for 3 seconds. Then, it will start joining the LoRaWAN networ[...]
Once the device has joined successfully, it will start uploading messages to The Things Stack, and you can see the messages in the Live data panel.

 

7.To decode the data to make it readable by human you can go to the payload decoder provided by Dragino. The link is:

https://github.com/dragino/dragino-end-node-decoder
Select the decoder according to the end device and copy the decoder supported by TTN.

After copying the decoder go to Payload formatter and select “custom Javascript formatter ”and paste it there.
 
8.To change the time interval between two uplinks you can go to messages and select downlink. select replace downlink queue.
FPort depends on the end device.
01 00 00 1E -30 sec 
01 00 003C  -1 minute
